Subject: [PATCH] belt: hand the route to the pi's on-body runtime and follow
 its position

the wearable that got built is a belt on a pca9685, driven by its own runtime on the pi. NUDGE_BELT_URL points us at it: nav start sends the route as /api/route returns it, calibrate lines the belt up and starts it, and its position is fed back to the navigator so speech, the hub and the caretaker follow the wearer. best effort throughout, like the collar: a belt that is off never breaks a walk. see docs/belt.md.
